{"actor":"Stephanie Schofield","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-09T09:17:35Z","event_type":"claimed","id":1569,"issue_id":"beth-gau.1","new_value":"{\"assignee\":\"Stephanie Schofield\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"beth-gau.1\",\"title\":\"Task 1: Add Skill Routing Table to Beth's Agent Definition\",\"description\":\"OBJECTIVE: Beth currently has ZERO skill references in beth.agent.md. When she works directly (simple tasks, quick fixes, or decides not to delegate), she operates without any domain knowledge from the skills directory. This task adds an explicit skill routing table so Beth knows which skills exist, which agents own them, and can reference them when working directly or instructing subagents.\\n\\nIMPLEMENTATION:\\n1. Open .github/agents/beth.agent.md\\n2. Add a new \\\"## Skill Routing\\\" section AFTER the \\\"## Your Team\\\" section and BEFORE \\\"## How You Operate\\\"\\n3. Insert this exact content:\\n\\n## Skill Routing\\n\\nWhen working directly or instructing subagents, load the appropriate skill for the domain:\\n\\n| Domain | Skill File | Primary Agent | Load When |\\n|--------|-----------|---------------|-----------|\\n| Requirements/PRD | `.github/skills/prd/SKILL.md` | product-manager | Defining features, writing specs |\\n| UI Components | `.github/skills/shadcn-ui/SKILL.md` | developer | Building UI with shadcn components |\\n| Framer Components | `.github/skills/framer-components/SKILL.md` | developer, ux-designer | Framer property controls, overrides |\\n| React Performance | `.github/skills/vercel-react-best-practices/SKILL.md` | developer | React/Next.js optimization |\\n| Security Analysis | `.github/skills/security-analysis/SKILL.md` | security-reviewer | Security audits, OWASP, threat models |\\n| Web Research | `.github/skills/web-search/SKILL.md` | researcher | Competitive analysis, market research |\\n| Design Audit | `.github/skills/web-design-guidelines/SKILL.md` | tester, ux-designer | UI review, accessibility audit |\\n| Azure Ops | `.github/skills/azure-operations/SKILL.md` | developer | Azure resource management |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n- When working directly on a task that falls in a skill domain, read the SKILL.md BEFORE starting work\\n- When spawning subagents, ALWAYS include \\\"Load and follow: \\u003cskill-path\\u003e\\\" for relevant skills in the prompt\\n- If a task spans multiple domains, load all relevant skills\\n\\n4. Apply the same change to templates/.github/agents/beth.agent.md\\n\\nFILES TO MODIFY:\\n- .github/agents/beth.agent.md (insert after ## Your Team table, before ## How You Operate)\\n- templates/.github/agents/beth.agent.md (mirror change)\\n\\nDEFINITION OF DONE:\\n- [ ] beth.agent.md contains ## Skill Routing section with complete routing table\\n- [ ] templates/ version mirrors the change exactly\\n- [ ] Table lists all 8 skills with correct file paths, agents, and trigger conditions\\n- [ ] Rules subsection instructs Beth to load skills when working directly AND when spawning subagents\\n- [ ] No other sections modified\\n- [ ] git diff shows only the expected additions\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":0,\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"owner\":\"sschofield@microsoft.com\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-09T06:39:41Z\",\"created_by\":\"Stephanie Schofield\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-09T06:39:41Z\"}"}
